      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HEDJET (8) got off the mark in style two back at Geelong when leading pillar-to-post and justifying his short quote. Had no peace last time on a wet deck and was tucked away on the inside, before popping off the fence in the straight and finishing off well into fourth. At his top now and is drawn to advantage. Suspect he gets the job done. MOUNT SABYINYO (1) is desperate to break through after two close finishes, the most recent as fav at Sale. At his top now but will need a clever ride from a sticky draw. SURPERB FROST (6) got the job done as favourite when resuming at Mornington. Tougher now but strips fitter and has more to offer stretching to the mile. Should be blending in at the right time.  SINISTER SAUCE (9) comes off a Kilmore win, gets meaningful weight relief and has an excellent jockey-horse record, but she's yet to fire a shot here in five starts. Prefer as a place chance.",
